Upstream-Name: smolhost
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/replghost/smolhost/issues
Source: https://github.com/replghost/smolhost
Corresponding-Source: https://github.com/replghost/smolhost/releases/download/v${upstream_version}/smolhost-v${upstream_version}-source.tar.gz

Smolhost declares GPL-3.0-or-later for its own code in Cargo.toml. The complete
upstream GPL version 3 text is installed at /usr/share/licenses/smolhost/LICENSE.
The upstream project does not supply a separate copyright-holder statement;
this packaging metadata does not assign copyright ownership to the maintainer
or to anyone else. Refer to the corresponding source for original notices.

Third-party components retain their respective copyrights and licenses.
The complete verbatim notices supplied in the upstream binary release are
installed under /usr/share/licenses/smolhost/third-party/licenses/.
The accompanying /usr/share/licenses/smolhost/third-party/dependencies.json
records each pinned dependency's upstream license expression, license-file
metadata, original registry package checksum and installed notice paths.
The inventory includes build, development and target-specific dependencies;
it does not claim that every listed component is linked into these binaries.
No third-party notice is replaced by this summary, and this is not a legal audit.

The public corresponding-source archive linked above contains the release's
source snapshot, locked vendored dependency sources and offline build inputs.
Release metadata and per-file hashes are retained at
/usr/share/doc/smolhost/upstream-release-manifest.json. The packaging operation
copies prebuilt binaries unchanged; it makes no reproducible-build claim.
